---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ImageResizer from '../components/ImageResizer';
---

<Layout
  title="Free Online Image Resizer & Converter"
  description="Resize, convert, and optimize images directly in your browser. Fast, free, and completely private with zero server uploads."
  path="/image-resizer"
>
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-8">
    <header class="mb-8 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-100 tracking-tight mb-3">
        Free Online Image Resizer &amp; Converter
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-slate-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        Change dimensions, adjust quality, and convert image formats locally on your computer.
        Your photos never leave your device.
      </p>
    </header>

    {/* Interactive React Island */}
    <ImageResizer client:load />

    {/* Explanatory, Answer-First SEO & Educational Content */}
    <article class="mt-12 space-y-10 text-slate-300">
      <section class="bg-slate-900/50 p-6 rounded-xl border border-slate-800">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-3">
          How Browser-Based Image Resizing Works
        </h2>
        <p class="leading-relaxed mb-3">
          Unlike traditional image utilities that upload your sensitive images to a cloud server,
          ImageTool utilizes high-performance browser APIs—including <strong>Web Workers</strong> and
          <strong>OffscreenCanvas</strong>.
        </p>
        <p class="leading-relaxed">
          When you select an image, its raw bytes are transferred to a background thread.
          The image is decoded, scaled using high-quality bicubic resampling, and re-encoded into your chosen format
          (WebP, JPEG, or PNG) without ever touching an external network endpoint.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-4">
          Step-by-Step: How to Resize and Convert an Image
        </h2>
        <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2.5 text-slate-300">
          <li><strong>Upload your image:</strong> Drag and drop your file or click the box to browse. Files up to 50 MB are supported.</li>
          <li><strong>Set your dimensions:</strong> Enter custom pixel dimensions or click one of the quick scale presets (25%, 50%, 75%, 200%). Keep aspect ratio locked to avoid distortion.</li>
          <li><strong>Select output format:</strong> Choose WebP for modern web performance, JPEG for photographs, or PNG for lossless transparency.</li>
          <li><strong>Click Resize &amp; Convert:</strong> The Web Worker will process your image in milliseconds.</li>
          <li><strong>Download:</strong> Click download to save your optimized file directly to your downloads folder.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-slate-900/40 p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-800">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200 mb-2">WebP (Recommended)</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
            Provides superior lossless and lossy compression. Produces files 25–35% smaller than comparable JPEGs at equivalent visual quality.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-900/40 p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-800">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200 mb-2">JPEG</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
            Universally compatible standard for complex photographs. Best suited for high-color images where transparency is not required.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-slate-900/40 p-4 rounded-lg border border-slate-800">
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200 mb-2">PNG</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
            Lossless format with full alpha transparency support. Ideal for logos, icons, screenshots, and graphics with sharp text.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-slate-800 pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-100 mb-6">
          Frequently Asked Questions
        </h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200 mb-1">
              Are my photos uploaded to any server?
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
              No. ImageTool adheres to a strict privacy-first architecture. All pixel manipulation and file encoding happen directly inside your web browser. No image data is sent across the internet.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200 mb-1">
              What is the maximum image resolution supported?
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
              You can process images up to 25 million pixels (for example, 5000 × 5000 pixels) and up to 50 MB in file size.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-slate-200 mb-1">
              Is ImageTool free to use?
            </h3>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
              Yes, 100% free with no account creation, subscriptions, or watermarks required.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
